  "description": {
    "text": "A file of nine cards sold in Japan from 10 December 1999 to mark the release of Pokémon Gold and Silver, ahead of the first Neo starter deck and expansion, Gold, Silver, to a New World..., which followed in February 2000. Its cards are the three Pokémon a player chooses from at the start of the games, Chikorita, Cyndaquil and Totodile, with their evolutions, all drawn by Ken Sugimori.\n\nThey are not the expansion's cards: each has its own art, HP and attacks, and none prints a rarity mark.",
